==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|de|Zeitgeber}}, from {{m|de|Zeit||time}} + {{m|de|Geber||giver}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtsʌɪtɡeɪbə/|/ˈzʌɪtɡeɪbə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|zeitgeber}}

# {{lb|en|physiology}} A rhythmically occurring [[cue]] given by the [[environment]], such as a change in [[light]] or [[temperature]], to reset the [[internal]] [[body clock]]. {{defdate|from 20th c.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2017|author={{w|Matthew Walker (scientist)|Matthew Walker}}|title=Why We Sleep|page=18|publisher=Penguin|year_published=2018
|passage=Thus, while light is the most reliable and thus the primary '''zeitgeber''', there are many factors that can be used in addition to, or in the absence of, daylight.}}